 ### [Surface Nets Mesh Generation](11602-surface-nets-mesh-generation.md)
-Generates a smooth triangle mesh from a binary density field or Signed Distance Field (SDF) by computing vertex positions at voxel centers based on local gradients, producing significantly fewer vertices and smoother geometry than blocky voxel-based methods. It serves as a bridge between raw voxel occupancy and high-fidelity surface extraction, offering a computationally efficient alternative to Marching Cubes when the input data is already structured as a grid.
